I focused on where in the RTL the instruction cache is instantiated and controlled, and how debug‐mode requests are generated and threaded through. To disable the I$ in debug, you need to

 1. Propagate the debug request signal into the fetch stage,
 2. Gate off the icache enable in the fetch stage,
 3. Ensure the icache itself respects that debug override,
 4. Wire the top-level core so the debug path reaches the I$.

That points at:

  – ibex_if_stage.sv      (where the I$ is turned on/off for fetch)  
  – ibex_icache.sv        (the I$ itself; must obey debug disable)  
  – ibex_debug_ctrl.sv    (produces the debug_req_i used to gate the I$)  
  – ibex_core.sv          (top-level where debug_ctrl → if_stage is hooked up)  

