│ This is inconsistent and can bias replacement behavior.            │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ From the provided context:                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  • In hpdcache_miss_handler.sv, PLRU/victim update on refill       │
│    already explicitly handles prefetches through:                  │
│    cfg_prefetch_updt_sel_victim_i                                  │
│    (seen in refill_updt_sel_victim_o logic).                       │
│  • In hpdcache_ctrl.sv, the directory PLRU update signal for       │
│    request-time behavior is forwarded as: .dir_updt_sel_victim_i   │
│    (st1_req_updt_sel_victim)                                       │
│    with no explicit prefetch-hit contribution visible in this      │
│    connection.                                                     │
│                                                                    │
│ So prefetch-miss path updates PLRU (via refill), while             │
│ prefetch-hit path misses PLRU update.                              │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep behavior config-driven (only update on prefetch when       │
│    prefetch-PLRU-update config is enabled).                        │
│  • Make a minimal, local change in control wiring rather than      │
│    changing larger FSM behavior.                                   │
│  • Avoid changing refill behavior (already correct for miss path). │
│  • Ensure no functional change for non-prefetch requests.          │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Augment the directory update select signal in hpdcache_ctrl.sv so  │
│ that, in addition to the existing control-engine update signal, it │
│ also triggers on:                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│  • valid stage-1 request,                                          │
│  • request is CMO_PREFETCH,                                        │
│  • prefetch PLRU update config enabled,                            │
│  • and the request is a cache hit (|st1_dir_hit_way).              │
│                                                                    │
│ This makes prefetch-hit behavior consistent with prefetch-miss     │
│ behavior under the same config.                                    │
