│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The RVFI probe interface expects PMP address CSR arrays as 32-bit  │
│ elements:                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • csr_pmpaddr_q_i[PMP_MAX_REGIONS] with each element [31:0].      │
│                                                                    │
│ But in RTL (cv32e40s_cs_registers.sv) PMP CSR address storage/read │
│ signals are sized with:                                            │
│                                                                    │
│  • PMP_ADDR_WIDTH = (PMP_GRANULARITY > 0) ? 33 - PMP_GRANULARITY : │
│    32                                                              │
│                                                                    │
│ So for G=3, PMP_ADDR_WIDTH=30, and wrapper connects a [29:0] array │
│ directly into a [31:0] array port. Xcelium rejects this            │
│ unpacked-array element width mismatch.                             │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  • In bhv/cv32e40s_wrapper.sv, RVFI connection:                    │
│     • .csr_pmpaddr_q_i ( core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_rdata )    │
│  • Underlying width source in rtl/cv32e40s_cs_registers.sv:        │
│     • localparam PMP_ADDR_WIDTH defines reduced signal width for   │
│       pmp_addr_*.                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep interface types consistent and explicit across module      │
│    boundaries.                                                     │
│  • Avoid simulator-dependent implicit conversions for unpacked     │
│    arrays.                                                         │
│  • Preserve architectural behavior for granularity-constrained low │
│    bits (hardwired zero behavior).                                 │
│  • Make minimal changes with low collateral impact.                │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • Make PMP_ADDR_WIDTH in CS registers 32 bits for RVFI-compatible │
│    observable CSR vectors.                                         │
│  • Preserve granularity semantics by explicitly zeroing low        │
│    non-implemented bits on write (pmp_addr_n assignment).          │
│                                                                    │
│ This fixes the type mismatch at the wrapper/RVFI boundary and      │
│ keeps CSR-visible values architecturally consistent for            │
│ granularity.                                                       │
│                                                                    │
