│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem                                                         │
│     • cv32e40s_wrapper connects RVFI PMP address probes directly   │
│       to core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_*.                         │
│     • Those CSR storage/readback signals are PMP_ADDR_WIDTH wide   │
│       (e.g. 30 bits when G=3), while RVFI currently declares PMP   │
│       address CSR probe inputs as 32-bit.                          │
│     • This causes:                                                 │
│        • Compile-time type mismatch (Xcelium strict type check),   │
│        • Incorrect RVFI CSR values in formal (implicit width       │
│          adaptation misrepresents pmpaddr).                        │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│     • Connection site in:                                          │
│        • bhv/cv32e40s_wrapper.sv (.csr_pmpaddr_n_i,                │
│          .csr_pmpaddr_q_i)                                         │
│     • RVFI interface declaration in:                               │
│        • bhv/cv32e40s_rvfi.sv (PMP CSR probe input widths)         │
│  3 Best-practice considerations                                    │
│     • Keep probe interface widths aligned with the producer signal │
│       widths (avoid implicit truncation/extension).                │
│     • Parameterize widths using architectural configuration (PMP   │
│       granularity) rather than hardcoding.                         │
│     • Avoid simulator-dependent implicit conversions for           │
│       formal/RTL observability paths.                              │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│     • In cv32e40s_rvfi, define PMP_ADDR_WIDTH from                 │
│       PMP_GRANULARITY.                                             │
│     • Change RVFI PMP CSR input probe widths from [31:0] to        │
│       [PMP_ADDR_WIDTH-1:0].                                        │
│     • This removes the wrapper type mismatch and preserves         │
│       correctly aligned PMP CSR data path semantics.               │
