╭─ Patch Generation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The RVFI hookup for PMP address CSRs is width-incompatible when    │
│ PMP_GRANULARITY (G) != 0.                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • RTL stores PMP address CSR internals in reduced width:          │
│     • pmp_addr_* : logic [PMP_ADDR_WIDTH-1:0]                      │
│     • where PMP_ADDR_WIDTH = (G > 0) ? 33-G : 32                   │
│  • RVFI interface expects full 32-bit CSR words:                   │
│     • csr_pmpaddr_*_i : logic [31:0] ...                           │
│                                                                    │
│ So with e.g. G=3, RTL is 30 bits and RVFI expects 32 bits, causing │
│ strict simulators (Xcelium) to fail elaboration.                   │
│                                                                    │
│ Also, semantically, directly zero-extending reduced-width storage  │
│ is wrong for CSR view: reduced storage corresponds to upper CSR    │
│ bits, so RVFI needs {stored_bits, zero_lsb_bits} (LSB padding),    │
│ not MSB zero-extension.                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ Primary mismatch is at wrapper RVFI connections in:                │
│                                                                    │
│  • bhv/cv32e40s_wrapper.sv                                         │
│     • .csr_pmpaddr_n_i ( core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_n )        │
│     • .csr_pmpaddr_q_i ( core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_rdata )    │
│                                                                    │
│ These connect reduced-width arrays directly into 32-bit RVFI       │
│ ports.                                                             │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep RVFI externally 32-bit for CSR architectural visibility.   │
│  • Do explicit width adaptation at integration boundary (wrapper), │
│    not by relying on implicit casting.                             │
│  • Preserve semantics by LSB-zero padding reduced PMP CSR          │
│    representation.                                                 │
│  • Keep changes minimal and localized.                             │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ In wrapper:                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • Introduce 32-bit adapted arrays for RVFI PMP addr probes.       │
│  • Fill them in a loop as:                                         │
│     • rvfi_pmpaddr_*[i] = {core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_*[i],    │
│       {(32-PMP_ADDR_WIDTH){1'b0}}};                                │
│  • Connect RVFI ports to these adapted arrays.                     │
│                                                                    │
│ This resolves both:                                                │
│                                                                    │
│  • compile-time type mismatch,                                     │
│  • incorrect RVFI CSR value encoding for non-zero granularity.     │
│                                                                    │
