│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is a feature gap in stream joining:                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • stream_join only supports joining all inputs.                   │
│  • It requires all selected input handshakes to happen             │
│    simultaneously.                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ Requested behavior:                                                │
│                                                                    │
│  • dynamically choose which inputs participate (mask/select),      │
│  • allow participating inputs to handshake independently over      │
│    multiple cycles,                                                │
│  • only produce the joined output handshake once all selected      │
│    inputs have handshaken once.                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where this should be addressed                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ From the provided context, there is no stream_join_dynamic         │
│ implementation yet, while stream_fork_dynamic exists conceptually  │
│ as the analogous feature on the fork side.                         │
│ So the fix is to provide a new IP: stream_join_dynamic.            │
│                                                                    │
│ Given available editable context, this is implemented by adding a  │
│ new module definition in src/stream_fork.sv (same compilation      │
│ unit), and documenting it in README.md.                            │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep existing IP behavior unchanged (stream_join, stream_fork   │
│    remain backward compatible).                                    │
│  • Add new functionality as a separate module                      │
│    (stream_join_dynamic) to avoid regressions.                     │
│  • Latch/track selected participants per in-flight join            │
│    transaction.                                                    │
│  • Ensure exactly one handshake per selected input per             │
│    transaction.                                                    │
│  • Block further input handshakes once join is complete and        │
│    waiting for downstream ready_i.                                 │
│  • Include parameter guard assertions (N_INP >= 1).                │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How the fix works                                               │
│                                                                    │
│ stream_join_dynamic adds:                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • sel_i: dynamic mask of inputs participating in current join.    │
│  • Per-transaction state:                                          │
│     • latched selection mask,                                      │
│     • bitmap of already-handshaken selected inputs.                │
│  • ready_o[k] is asserted independently for each selected,         │
│    not-yet-seen input.                                             │
│  • valid_o is asserted once all selected inputs are seen.          │
│  • When valid_o && ready_i, transaction completes and state clears │
│    for next dynamic selection.                                     │
