│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue requests a join primitive with two capabilities that     │
│ current stream_join does not provide:                              │
│                                                                    │
│  • Dynamic subset selection of input streams to participate in a   │
│    join transaction.                                               │
│  • Independent input handshakes, i.e., each selected input may     │
│    complete at different cycles, and the output fires once all     │
│    selected inputs have completed.                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ This is effectively the “specular” counterpart of dynamic forking  │
│ behavior.                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where this maps in the current code context                     │
│                                                                    │
│  • src/stream_fork.sv already contains sequential                  │
│    handshake-tracking logic for independent completion across      │
│    multiple outputs (fork side).                                   │
│  • There is currently no corresponding dynamic+independent join    │
│    implementation in the provided context.                         │
│  • README.md lists available IPs and currently has no              │
│    stream_join_dynamic entry.                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep the existing stream_fork behavior unchanged.               │
│  • Add a new IP module rather than breaking compatibility of       │
│    existing stream_join.                                           │
│  • Keep logic simple and robust:                                   │
│     • Track per-input completion state (done_q).                   │
│     • Latch selection for the active transaction.                  │
│     • Assert output valid only once all selected inputs have       │
│       completed.                                                   │
│     • Reset state cleanly on output handshake.                     │
│  • Add basic parameter sanity assertion (N_INP >= 1).              │
│  • Update documentation table to expose the new IP.                │
