Based on the description, the core of the bug lives in the multi‐bank L2 memory IP, where only 2 LSBs (for 32-bit word alignment) are stripped off instead of also removing the extra `$clog2(N_BANKS)` bits used for bank selection. In PULP’s RTL hierarchy the bulk of that lives in the L2 RAM IP directory, with the parameter definitions, the actual multi-bank implementation, and the small wrapper and interconnect files that hook the banks together.

Here are the four files that will most likely need fixes (in order of importance):

```plaintext
hw/ip/l2_ram/l2_ram_multibank.sv
hw/ip/l2_ram/l2_ram_pkg.sv
hw/ip/l2_ram/l2_ram_wrapper.sv
hw/ip/interconnect/memory_interconnect.sv
