I looked at where `adbg_lintonly_top` is instantiated (in `lint_jtag_wrap.sv`) and saw that its new port `lint_r_aux_i` never gets driven. To remove the lint warning you must either tie that port off where it’s instantiated, remove/modify it in the wrapper module, or change the rtl that defines it. That points at these four files as the ones you’ll need to edit (in order of priority):

```  
rtl/pulp_soc/lint_jtag_wrap.sv
rtl/pulp_soc/adbg_lintonly_top.sv
rtl/pulp_soc/dbg_module.sv
rtl/pulp_soc/lint_jtag_wrap_tb.sv
```  
- In lint_jtag_wrap.sv you can hook up or default‐tie off the new port.  
- In adbg_lintonly_top.sv it’s declared/forwarded to dbg_module_i.  
- In dbg_module.sv you could remove or repurpose the now‐unused input if you decide it’s obsolete.  
- Finally update the testbench so it matches your changed instantiation and no longer trips on the unconnected port.
