124 ## Customization
125 
126 The debug system can be configured at synthesis time through parameters.
127 
128 **Parameter Name** | **Valid values** | **Default** | **Description**
129 ------------------ | ---------------- | ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
130 NrHarts            | 1..2^20          | 1           | Number of connected harts
131 BusWidth           | 32, 64           | 32          | Bus width (for debug memory and SBA busses)
132 SelectableHarts    |                  | 1           | Bitmask to select physically available harts for systems that don't use hart numbers in a contiguous fashion.
133 
134 In addition to these parameters, additional configuration is provided through top-level signals, which are expected to be set to a fixed value at synthesis time.
135 
136 Signal Name | Data Type  | Width   | Description
137 ----------- | ---------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
138 hartinfo    | hartinfo_t | NrHarts | Value of the hartinfo DM register, see the RISC-V Debug Specification v0.13, Section 3.14.2 for details. **nscratch**: Number of debug scratch registers. Must be set to 2. **dataaccess**: Must be set to 1. (The data register are shadowed in the hart's memory.) **datasize**: Must be set to `dm::DataCount`. **dataaddr**: Must be set to `dm::DataAddr` (0x380).
139 
140 **SystemVerilog definition of the hartinfo_t structure**
141 
142 ```verilog
143 typedef struct packed {
144   logic [31:24] zero1;
145   logic [23:20] nscratch;
146   logic [19:17] zero0;
147   logic         dataaccess;
148   logic [15:12] datasize;
149   logic [11:0]  dataaddr;
