35 
36 The functionality of the debug system is implemented according to the RISC-V Debug Specification.
37 Refer to this document for more information.
38 
39 ## Block Diagram
40 
41 ![Block diagram of the debug system](debugsys_schematic.svg)
42 
43 ## Debug Module Registers
44 
45 An external debugger performs all interaction with the Debug Module through a register interface, accessed over a dedicated bus, the Debug Module Interface (DMI).
46 The registers are called "Debug Module Registers" and defined in the RISC-V Debug Specification, Section 3.14.
47 Our implementation only provides a single Debug Module on the DMI bus mapped to base address 0, hence all addresses below can be considered absolute.
48 
49 **Address** | **Name**                                     | **Implementation Notes**
50 ----------- | -------------------------------------------- | ------------------------
51 0x04        | Abstract Data 0 (data0)
52 0x0f        | Abstract Data 11 (data11)
53 0x10        | Debug Module Control (dmcontrol)             | see table below
54 0x11        | Debug Module Status (dmstatus)               | see table below
55 0x12        | Hart Info (hartinfo)
56 0x13        | Halt Summary 1 (haltsum1)
57 0x14        | Hart Array Window Select (hawindowsel)
58 0x15        | Hart Array Window (hawindow)
</code>
